# Coding Style

## Python
- Type hints on all public functions with return types
- Docstrings on all public classes and methods
- Max 500 lines per file, 50 lines per function — split if larger
- Imports: stdlib → third-party → frappe → local
- Never bare `except:` — catch specific exceptions
- Prefer composition over inheritance for channel adapters

## JavaScript / React
- Functional components with hooks only — no class components
- TypeScript preferred for new files
- Named exports for shared components, default for page components
- Props interface defined with TypeScript types

## Tailwind
- Use design tokens from tailwind.config.js
- No arbitrary values like `w-[347px]` — use closest token
- Mobile-first responsive: `sm:`, `md:`, `lg:` breakpoints
- Dark mode via `dark:` prefix

## General
- Commit messages: imperative mood, under 72 chars
- Branch naming: `feature/xxx`, `fix/xxx`, `refactor/xxx`
- Never commit to main or develop directly
